{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Come to Pharaoh.</b> To his palace. R. Judah HaLevi said: there were two plagues in water — the first, that [the waters] turned red and the fish died, and the second, that the frogs came up from them. And two on land: one from the vermin and the second from the 'arov, and they are mixed wild animals, as written, ותוצא הארץ נפש חיה (Genesis 1:24). And two in the air, for the thing was nothing but hot or cold, different from the norm, and in one moment uncounted ones die, because the spirit of all life, which is in the heart, depends on the air. And the second: the plague of boils, for Scripture calls the firmament that is over their heads 'heavens.' And the seventh plague is mixed from the sphere of storm and from the sphere of fire, and likewise written, ואש מתלקחת בתוך הברד (Exodus 9:24). And the eighth, the plague of locusts, which came from afar by means of the wind. And the ninth was a wondrous plague: the light of the two luminaries and the stars disappeared from the land of Egypt. And the tenth, the descent of the destroyer from the spheres of glory to kill the firstborn."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:51.548181597Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}